    "lawCode": "Amd §168-a, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1505\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to establishing Women's\nEquality Day\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo establish Women's Equality Day as a Day of Commemoration.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 -- Amends subdivision 3 of section 168-a of the Executive\nLaw to establish August 26 as Women's Equality Day, a Day of\nCommemoration.\n\nSection 2 -- Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nWomen's Equality Day commemorates the adoption of the 19th Amendment\nto the US Constitution. The adoption of this Amendment guaranteed that\nwomen would have the right to vote, and it can truly be called a\nturning point in American history.\n\nSince the adoption of the 19th Amendment, women have taken leadership\nroles in business, politics, journalism, and many other areas of\nAmerican life.\n\nBy enacting this bill into law, New York State can properly recognize\nthe great contributions of women to the strength and vitality of our\nState and Nation.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nS.6914-A/A.10527-A of 2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThirty days after this act shall have become a law.\n",
